SUMMARY: Fast Friends: Meet New People\, Make Connections & Play 50+ Board
  Games | 25–45
DESCRIPTION:Toronto 20's to 50's Singles Social (4000+)\nLooking for a bet
 ter way to spend a Saturday evening in Toronto than sitting at home wonder
 ing how to expand your social circle?\n\nFast Friends gives you an easy st
 arting point. Instead of walking into a busy pub and hoping you happen to 
 meet the right people\, our host creates the structure — guiding convers
 ations and rotations so you can meet a variety of people naturally\, even 
 if you arrive on your own.\n\nAnd this time\, we’re back at Stout Irish 
 Pub — a relaxed Toronto pub where the socialising can continue long afte
 r the hosted rounds finish\, with drinks\, food and 50+ board games to cho
 ose from. 🎲🍻\n\n🎟️ Book Early & Save: [https://toronto10thoct.e
 ventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto10thoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\n\nYou can pay s
 ecurely online with any debit or credit card through PayPal — no PayPal 
 account required.\n*Advance tickets are cheaper and help us plan the right
  space and group size for a comfortable evening.*\n\nEarly Bird: CAD $10 \
 \| Regular: CAD $15 \\| At the Door: CAD $20 cash\n\n🤝 The Evening\n7:0
 0 PM — Welcome & Settle In\nMeet your host\, Kristabelle\, grab a drink 
 and get comfortable.\nWhether you've just moved to Toronto or have been he
 re for years\, this is a chance to step out of your usual routine and meet
  some different people.\nComing alone? That's completely fine — most gue
 sts do.\n\n7:30–8:30 PM — Fast Friends\nForget the usual “How do I s
 tart talking to someone?” moment.\nOur host guides a series of short con
 versations and rotations\, giving you the chance to meet different people 
 throughout the evening. You don't need to plan what happens next — just 
 show up\, join the conversation and see who you connect with.\n\n✨ Theme
 d Connection Rounds\nWe'll mix things up with interactive prompts and them
 ed conversation challenges that help uncover common interests and unexpect
 ed connections.\nFrom travel and food to music\, books\, hobbies and weeke
 nd adventures\, these rounds are designed to get you talking about somethi
 ng more interesting than small talk.\n\n🎲 8:30 PM onwards — 50+ Board
  Games & Socialising\nThis is where Stout really adds something special.\n
 Once the hosted rounds finish\, you don't have to call it a night. Stout h
 as 50+ board games available\, giving you an easy way to continue socialis
 ing with the people you've just met.\nPick a game\, join a group\, grab an
 other drink\, or simply keep chatting. You can make the evening as relaxed
  and spontaneous as you like.\n\n❤️ Why Come Along?\n✔️ Meet 20+ n
 ew people in one evening\n✔️ Guided conversations make it easier to co
 nnect\n✔️ Interactive themed rounds to spark better conversations\n✔
 ️ 50+ board games at Stout 🎲\n✔️ Relaxed Irish pub atmosphere\n
 ✔️ Reserved space for our group\n✔️ Members from our Toronto Meetu
 p communities may also join\n✔️ Most guests come solo\n✔️ Designed
  for ladies and gents aged 25–45\n✔️ Friendship-focused — not a da
 ting event\n\n📍 Why Stout Irish Pub?\nLocated at 221 Carlton Street\, S
 tout is an easy-to-reach Toronto pub with a relaxed atmosphere\, drinks\, 
 food and one of the best extras for a social event — a huge selection of
  50+ board games.\nSo you can start the evening with structured conversati
 ons and finish it however you want: playing\, chatting\, laughing or getti
 ng to know someone you clicked with.\n\n👥 Who Is It For?\nYou don't nee
 d to be new to Toronto\, part of an existing group or know anyone attendin
 g.\nIf your social circle could use some fresh faces — whether you're ne
 w in town or simply ready to meet people outside your usual routine — yo
 u're welcome.\n\nCome by yourself\, bring a friend\, or do both.\n\n🌍 A
 bout Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years\, Fast Friends has been creating oppo
 rtunities for people to connect through professionally hosted social event
 s in 30+ cities worldwide.\n\nOur goal is simple: make meeting people easi
 er and give you a reason to actually start the conversation.\nCome solo. W
 e'll guide the experience. You make the connections. ❤️
